{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01271",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.4,
      "end_seconds": 7.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "Hi, um, is it okay to come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.78,
      "end_seconds": 12.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 14.47,
      "end_seconds": 20.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. I'll stay and fill in anything that's missed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.92,
      "end_seconds": 24.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "So, good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.55,
      "end_seconds": 36.37,
      "duration_seconds": 10.82,
      "text": "Uh, mainly a dry tickly cough. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.26,
      "end_seconds": 44.74,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.32,
      "end_seconds": 49.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "It's been about a year, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.97,
      "end_seconds": 53.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Is it worse at certain times?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.77,
      "end_seconds": 60.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Okay, so I notice it more with lying down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.75,
      "end_seconds": 63.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "How much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.45,
      "end_seconds": 70.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.53,
      "end_seconds": 76.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.71,
      "end_seconds": 82.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Uh, you know, about a four out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.71,
      "end_seconds": 86.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "What eases it, if anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.61,
      "end_seconds": 91.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Only sips of water, and it's not much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.86,
      "end_seconds": 95.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.2,
      "end_seconds": 105.09,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "Mm, it's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.01,
      "end_seconds": 115.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.18,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.24,
      "end_seconds": 119.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "It, It comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.38,
      "end_seconds": 124.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.46,
      "end_seconds": 131.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "A little breathlessness goes along with it, most of the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.08,
      "end_seconds": 141.41,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "Um, and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 141.51,
      "end_seconds": 147.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.02,
      "end_seconds": 159.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.57,
      "text": "Right, I was getting to that! Actually, and I've been coughing at night as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.22,
      "end_seconds": 164.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "So, how much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.11,
      "end_seconds": 172.24,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "I'd call it severe. The little breathlessness? That's been for three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.93,
      "end_seconds": 175.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "How often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.59,
      "end_seconds": 194.51,
      "duration_seconds": 17.92,
      "text": "It comes and goes. Sorry, what was I saying, as for tickle at the back of my throat, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.23,
      "end_seconds": 199.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.72,
      "end_seconds": 203.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "I'd call it mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 204.48,
      "end_seconds": 206.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Yes, exactly like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.0,
      "end_seconds": 213.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any chest pain, weight loss or wheeze?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.05,
      "end_seconds": 220.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "I haven't had chest pain, weight loss or wheeze, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.35,
      "end_seconds": 224.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Have you had fever, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.49,
      "end_seconds": 233.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Hmm, um, not that I've noticed, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.55,
      "end_seconds": 239.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any heartburn or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.73,
      "end_seconds": 247.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "Right, no heartburn or coughing up blood, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.49,
      "end_seconds": 250.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.95,
      "end_seconds": 254.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.3,
      "end_seconds": 259.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.34,
      "end_seconds": 264.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "So, my daughter has type 1 diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.7,
      "end_seconds": 268.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.14,
      "end_seconds": 278.77,
      "duration_seconds": 6.63,
      "text": "Right, I had keyhole surgery on my gallbladder two years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.65,
      "end_seconds": 294.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.11,
      "end_seconds": 305.22,
      "duration_seconds": 8.11,
      "text": "I have acid reflux, for about ten years. I've had high blood pressure, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.05,
      "end_seconds": 318.07,
      "duration_seconds": 12.02,
      "text": "Right, so acid reflux and high blood pressure are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 319.6,
      "end_seconds": 330.43,
      "duration_seconds": 10.83,
      "text": "Well, it's lansoprazole, 30 milligrams, before breakfast, doctor. Yeah, it's lisinopril, once a day for my pressure, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.1,
      "end_seconds": 333.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 337.86,
      "end_seconds": 338.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "10 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.76,
      "end_seconds": 344.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.55,
      "end_seconds": 353.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "No, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 354.24,
      "end_seconds": 361.3,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "Hold on, doctor, I think she reacted to erythromycin once. I'm not certain, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 363.1,
      "end_seconds": 367.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Maybe, um, but I don't recall it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 369.22,
      "end_seconds": 374.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "Okay, I'll note both of those. Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 376.9,
      "end_seconds": 380.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 385.22,
      "end_seconds": 395.0,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Temperature is 36.8 degrees, saturation 97 percent, pressure 116 over 77, respiratory rate 17, pulse 79."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 396.97,
      "end_seconds": 398.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 399.61,
      "end_seconds": 403.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 413.16,
      "end_seconds": 414.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 416.29,
      "end_seconds": 418.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 431.59,
      "end_seconds": 435.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Your chest is clear and there is no wheeze."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 437.87,
      "end_seconds": 459.14,
      "duration_seconds": 21.27,
      "text": "You can relax now. Having listened and examined, this is probably a persistent dry cough without a clear cause so far. Another possibility is post-nasal drip. Another possibility is reflux. Just to be sure I understood. You've had a dry tickly cough for about a year, and no weight loss or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 459.83,
      "end_seconds": 461.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 462.94,
      "end_seconds": 493.9,
      "duration_seconds": 30.96,
      "text": "We should do a chest X-ray for chronic cough. A breathing test is what I'd like next, for cough. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. We will review your tablets and see whether the cough settles over a month. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. Book a review in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 494.59,
      "end_seconds": 498.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 499.06,
      "end_seconds": 503.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Okay, um, so alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}